WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.769 --> 00:00:17.473
After leaving Patty's Place, Anne and Priscilla went straight to Phil's boardinghouse to tell her the good news.

2
00:00:17.493 --> 00:00:20.695
"Well, what has happened to you two?

3
00:00:21.456 --> 00:00:23.117
Why, you're actually shining!

4
00:00:23.998 --> 00:00:24.518
What's up?"

5
00:00:24.859 --> 00:00:26.360
Phil said when she answered the door.

6
00:00:27.468 --> 00:00:32.931
"Priscilla and I are going to live in Patty's Place next winter," said Anne triumphantly.

7
00:00:32.951 --> 00:00:41.236
"We've rented it," Priscilla continued, "and our friend Stella Maynard is coming, and she's moving in with us!"

8
00:00:42.276 --> 00:00:45.498
Suddenly Phil got down on her knees before Anne and Priscilla.

9
00:00:45.518 --> 00:00:47.659
"Oh, please let me come too!

10
00:00:48.539 --> 00:00:49.400
I'll be so good.

11
00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:53.662
If there's no room for me, I'll sleep in the little doghouse in the backyard!

12
00:00:54.383 --> 00:00:56.524
Please let me be your roommate!"

13
00:00:58.348 --> 00:00:59.329
"Get up, silly!"

14
00:00:59.809 --> 00:01:00.529
said Anne.

15
00:01:01.350 --> 00:01:06.633
She then said slowly, "Phil, we'd love that, but I'll be honest.

16
00:01:07.693 --> 00:01:11.595
I'm poor, Priscilla is poor, Stella Maynard is poor.

17
00:01:12.456 --> 00:01:14.997
The house and food will be simple and plain.

18
00:01:15.958 --> 00:01:21.381
You come from a wealthy family, and you live in an expensive boardinghouse, with fancy meals.

19
00:01:22.382 --> 00:01:26.444
Are you sure that you want a simple life, living with poor students?"

20
00:01:28.152 --> 00:01:29.452
"Oh, what do I care?"

21
00:01:29.973 --> 00:01:31.253
said Phil dramatically.

22
00:01:31.273 --> 00:01:37.054
"I'd live on bread and water—with just a little jam—if you'll let me move in."

23
00:01:37.074 --> 00:01:42.896
"Well, Phil, there would also be many chores to do," Anne continued.

24
00:01:42.916 --> 00:01:50.238
"At the moment you have a maid, but at Patty's Place, you would have to—" "I'll learn how

25
00:01:50.278 --> 00:01:51.158
to cook and clean!"

26
00:01:51.979 --> 00:01:52.799
Phil interrupted.

27
00:01:52.819 --> 00:01:57.120
"There's just one more thing," said Priscilla.

28
00:01:58.004 --> 00:02:02.908
"As all Redmond students know, Phil, you entertain visitors almost every evening.

29
00:02:03.828 --> 00:02:05.690
You have a very busy social life.

30
00:02:06.610 --> 00:02:09.152
Now at Patty's Place, we can't do that.

31
00:02:09.973 --> 00:02:13.175
We have decided we'll have visitors on Friday evenings only.

32
00:02:13.195 --> 00:02:14.856
How does that sound?"

33
00:02:14.876 --> 00:02:17.978
"Oh, that's fine," said Phil.

34
00:02:17.998 --> 00:02:22.902
"I knew I should have had a rule like that, but I couldn't decide on what day!

35
00:02:22.922 --> 00:02:25.504
You know how indecisive I am!"

36
00:02:27.436 --> 00:02:32.538
"Well," said Anne, "of course, we must check with Stella, but I'm sure she'll agree."

37
00:02:32.558 --> 00:02:38.261
"And if you get tired of our simple life, you can move out of Patty's Place, and no

38
00:02:38.321 --> 00:02:40.362
questions asked," added Priscilla.

39
00:02:42.202 --> 00:02:46.744
Phil hugged them both jubilantly, and Anne and Priscilla went home to the boardinghouse.

40
00:02:46.764 --> 00:02:51.066
"I hope things will be all right," said Priscilla soberly.

41
00:02:51.086 --> 00:02:55.188
"Phil's a great friend, but how will she be to live with?"

42
00:02:56.128 --> 00:02:58.230
"Who knows how any of us will get along?"

43
00:02:58.650 --> 00:02:59.451
Anne pointed out.

44
00:02:59.471 --> 00:03:03.975
"It's not as if Phil is selfish; she's just a little thoughtless.

45
00:03:04.896 --> 00:03:06.097
I think it will be fun!"

46
00:03:07.759 --> 00:03:11.082
At the end of the term, Anne won the English scholarship.

47
00:03:11.902 --> 00:03:16.206
She was overjoyed since she could now support herself and not rely on Marilla.

48
00:03:17.167 --> 00:03:19.309
Anne went back to Avonlea for the vacation.

49
00:03:20.350 --> 00:03:25.599
People told Anne she hadn't changed much, in a tone that hinted they were surprised and a little

50
00:03:25.639 --> 00:03:27.100
disappointed that she hadn't.

51
00:03:28.282 --> 00:03:30.023
Avonlea had not changed either.

52
00:03:30.984 --> 00:03:32.426
At least, so it seemed.

53
00:03:34.948 --> 00:03:38.491
But then Anne learned that Billy Andrews had married Nettie Blewett.

54
00:03:39.452 --> 00:03:41.514
She saw them together in church on Sunday.

55
00:03:42.455 --> 00:03:44.758
Anne's real surprise, though, was Ruby Gillis.

56
00:03:45.799 --> 00:03:46.880
What had happened to her?

57
00:03:47.904 --> 00:03:53.189
She was as beautiful as ever, but her blue eyes were too bright, her cheeks were too flushed,

58
00:03:53.549 --> 00:03:54.710
and she was very thin.

59
00:03:54.730 --> 00:03:58.553
"Is Ruby Gillis sick?

60
00:03:59.294 --> 00:04:01.976
She looks so different," Anne said to Mrs.

61
00:04:02.036 --> 00:04:03.657
Lynde as they walked home from church.

62
00:04:04.658 --> 00:04:06.239
Marilla frowned and looked sad.

63
00:04:07.060 --> 00:04:11.484
Mrs. Lynde said bluntly, "Ruby Gillis is dying of tuberculosis.

64
00:04:12.484 --> 00:04:14.886
Everybody knows it except Ruby and her family.

65
00:04:15.847 --> 00:04:16.648
They won't admit it.

66
00:04:17.668 --> 00:04:20.589
If you ask them about Ruby, they say she's perfectly healthy."

67
00:04:22.649 --> 00:04:24.330
Anne listened in shocked silence.

68
00:04:25.270 --> 00:04:28.031
Ruby Gillis, her old school friend, dying?

69
00:04:28.811 --> 00:04:29.711
Could it be possible?

70
00:04:30.612 --> 00:04:35.053
In recent years they had grown apart, and Ruby and Anne had not talked as much as they

71
00:04:35.173 --> 00:04:35.593
used to.

72
00:04:36.653 --> 00:04:41.654
But the old schoolgirl friendship was still there—fun, beautiful, silly Ruby!

73
00:04:42.595 --> 00:04:46.996
It was impossible to think of her and something as tragic as death in the same thought.

74
00:04:48.700 --> 00:04:52.381
Ruby had greeted Anne after church and urged her to come visit the next day.

75
00:04:52.401 --> 00:04:58.023
Anne had agreed, and so the next evening, Diana and Anne walked to the Gillis' house.

76
00:04:58.043 --> 00:05:04.284
"It's so awful to hear Ruby chatting and pretending nothing is wrong," Diana told Anne.

77
00:05:04.304 --> 00:05:08.945
"Sometimes she can hardly speak because she's coughing so much."

78
00:05:10.806 --> 00:05:16.007
Diana and Anne arrived at the Gillis' home, where many young male visitors had already arrived.

79
00:05:16.948 --> 00:05:23.644
Everyone was in the parlor, and two young men from Avonlea, Leonard Kimball and Alan Bell, were competing

80
00:05:23.684 --> 00:05:24.725
for Ruby's attention.

81
00:05:25.686 --> 00:05:29.009
Ruby was dressed in white, and her eyes and cheeks were bright.

82
00:05:29.949 --> 00:05:33.412
She giggled and chatted with her male admirers for most of the evening.

83
00:05:34.933 --> 00:05:39.737
At one point Ruby took Anne upstairs to her bedroom to show Anne some of her new summer

84
00:05:39.777 --> 00:05:42.640
clothes. "How do you like my new white hat?

85
00:05:43.480 --> 00:05:44.721
It's the latest fashion.

86
00:05:45.582 --> 00:05:47.624
I liked the hat you wore to church yesterday."

87
00:05:48.496 --> 00:05:51.419
She turned, holding the hat to her head with one hand.

88
00:05:51.439 --> 00:05:55.282
"Anne, did you see those two Avonlea boys downstairs?

89
00:05:56.463 --> 00:05:59.485
They're nice, but Tony Spencer is the one I really like.

90
00:06:00.366 --> 00:06:01.507
He couldn't come tonight."

91
00:06:03.328 --> 00:06:05.010
Ruby gave a shallow little laugh.

92
00:06:05.991 --> 00:06:08.553
Anne looked at the ground; she didn't know what to say.

93
00:06:09.433 --> 00:06:14.297
Just for a moment her eyes met Ruby's, and Anne saw something that made her heart ache.

94
00:06:14.317 --> 00:06:17.380
"Come and see me while you're home, please, Anne?"

95
00:06:17.684 --> 00:06:18.465
whispered Ruby.

96
00:06:18.485 --> 00:06:20.006
"I want to see you.

97
00:06:20.847 --> 00:06:25.611
I've missed having an old friend like you around "Are you feeling all right, Ruby?"

98
00:06:26.012 --> 00:06:26.592
Anne asked.

99
00:06:26.612 --> 00:06:29.475
"Me?" Ruby replied.

100
00:06:29.495 --> 00:06:31.717
"Why, I'm perfectly healthy, Anne.

101
00:06:32.678 --> 00:06:36.721
Of course, last winter I had the flu, and I had a slow recovery, but now I am

102
00:06:36.761 --> 00:06:37.182
all right.

103
00:06:38.063 --> 00:06:39.284
I don't look sick, surely?"

104
00:06:40.285 --> 00:06:43.808
Ruby's voice was almost bitter, as if Anne had accused her of something.

105
00:06:44.744 --> 00:06:49.754
Then Ruby went quickly downstairs and talked just to the young men, as if Anne and Diana were

106
00:06:49.794 --> 00:06:50.235
not there.
